023)","Perez et al. (2022)","here","here","here","Mehrabi et al. 2023","in-context learning","Perez et al. 2022","Schramowski et al. 2022","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","Perspective API","#","#","Madry et al. 2017","#","Xie et al. 2023","Jain et al. 2023","White-box attacks","UAT-LM","Jain et al. 2023","#","#","â€œTowards Deep Learning Models Resistant to Adversarial Attacksâ€","â€œSemantically equivalent adversarial rules for debugging NLP modelsâ€","â€œGradient-based adversarial attacks against text transformersâ€","â€œHotFlip: White-Box Adversarial Examples for Text Classificationâ€","â€œUniversal Adversarial Triggers for Attacking and Analyzing NLP.â€","code","â€œRobust Conversational Agents against Imperceptible Toxicity Triggers.â€","â€œUniversal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models.â€","â€œRLPrompt: Optimizing Discrete Text Prompts with Reinforcement Learning.â€","â€œIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language Attack on Text Classification and Entailment.â€","â€œBERT-Attack: Adversarial Attack Against BERT Using BERT.â€","\"TextAttack: A Framework for Adversarial Attacks, Data Augmentation, and Adversarial Training in NLP.\"","â€œBot-Adversarial Dialogue for Safe Conversational Agents.â€","â€œAdversarial training for high-stakes reliability.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models with Language Models.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.â€","â€œFLIRT: Feedback Loop In-context Red Teaming.â€","â€œExplore, Establish, Exploit: Red Teaming Language Models from Scratch.â€","â€œDefending ChatGPT against Jailbreak Attack via Self-Reminder.â€","â€œAutomatically Auditing Large Language Models via Discrete Optimization.â€","â€œCompromising Real-World LLM-Integrated Applications with Indirect Prompt Injection.â€","â€œBaseline Defenses for Adversarial Attacks Against Aligned Language Models.â€","â€œJailbroken: How Does LLM Safety Training Fail?â€","â€œEDA: Easy data augmentation techniques for boosting performance on text classification tasks.â€","www.jailbreakchat.com","â€œYou can use GPT-4 to create prompt injections against GPT-4â€","Nlp","Language-Model","Safety","Adversarial Attacks","Robustness","Redteam"],"orig_elements":"","emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","â†’Which","NOUN","WP","is â†’","WP","â€™sâ€™","wasâ†’is","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","â€œa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.â€","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"chroma:document":"The above token search method can be augmented with beam search. When looking for the optimal token embedding $\\mathbf{e}â€™_i$, we can pick top-$k$ candidates instead of a single one, searching from left to right and score each beam by $\\mathcal{L}_\\text{adv}$ on the current data batch.\n\nThe design of the loss $\\mathcal{L}_\\text{adv}$ for UAT is task-specific. Classification or reading comprehension relies on cross entropy. In their experiment, conditional text generation is configured to maximize the likelihood of a language model $p$ generating similar content to a set of bad outputs $\\mathcal{Y}_\\text{bad}$ given any user input:","link_urls":["#token-manipulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2022-04-15-data-gen/#EDA","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500.pdf","#gradient-based-attacks","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144","https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09675","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","#hotflip","https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.15980","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08774","#UAT","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","#jailbreak-prompting","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/3d318387-903a-422c-8347-8e12768c14b5","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/4f37a029-9dff-4862-b323-c96a5504de5d","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","#humans-in-the-loop-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","https://sites.google.com/view/qanta/resources","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","#BERT-Attack","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://github.com/anthropics/hh-rlhf/tree/master/red-team-attempts","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/gpt-4.pdf","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/DALL_E_3_System_Card.pdf","#model-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2018-04-08-policy-gradient/